[Task Description]
Define rules that tensorflow.math.bessel_i0 API parameters should satisfy. Refer to the API documentation. Particularly, there should be at least one rule to suppress each error message.

Type is encoded as an integer (index of the following list):
[bool, np.int8, np.int16, np.int32, np.int64, np.uint8, np.float16, np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128, str, np.dtype]

String value should be selected from the following list:
["ii", "ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba", "none", "sum", "max", "min", "prod", "relu", "tanh", "sigmoid", "softmax", "elu", "selu", "gelu", "swish", "softplus", "linear", "valid", "same", "causal", "channels_last", "channels_first"]

[API Documentation]
Computes the Bessel i0 function of `x` element-wise.

  Modified Bessel function of order 0.

  It is preferable to use the numerically stabler function `i0e(x)` instead.

  >>> tf.math.special.bessel_i0([-1., -0.5, 0.5, 1.]).numpy()
  array([1.26606588, 1.06348337, 1.06348337, 1.26606588], dtype=float32)

  Args:
    x: A `Tensor` or `SparseTensor`. Must be one of the following types: `half`,
      `float32`, `float64`.
    name: A name for the operation (optional).

  Returns:
    A `Tensor` or `SparseTensor`, respectively. Has the same type as `x`.

  @compatibility(scipy)
  Equivalent to scipy.special.i0
  @end_compatibility

[API Signature] x: tensor, name: string

